#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/14-iot_Bluetooth_oled.rst:17
msgid "14. Bluetooth OLED"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/14-iot_Bluetooth_oled.rst:26
msgid "Type on the phone, read it on a 128 x 64 OLED display. This project is close to the LCD one, but the display is smaller and the sketch has to guess when a sentence is finished - the phone sends characters one after another, not as one block."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/14-iot_Bluetooth_oled.rst:32
msgid "1. Build the Circuit"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/14-iot_Bluetooth_oled.rst:36
msgid "The module draws a high current at start-up, so make sure the 9 V battery or an external power supply is plugged into the DC jack of the R4 Minima."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/14-iot_Bluetooth_oled.rst:42
msgid ":ref:`cpn_uno`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/14-iot_Bluetooth_oled.rst:43
msgid ":ref:`cpn_espc201`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/14-iot_Bluetooth_oled.rst:44
msgid ":ref:`cpn_olde`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/14-iot_Bluetooth_oled.rst:48
msgid "2. Upload the Code"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/14-iot_Bluetooth_oled.rst:50
msgid "Open the ``14-Bluetooth_oled.ino`` file under the path of ``ultimate-sensor-kit\\code\\iot_project_espc201\\bluetooth\\14-Bluetooth_oled``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/14-iot_Bluetooth_oled.rst:54
msgid "Install **Adafruit SSD1306** and **Adafruit GFX Library** from the Library Manager."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/14-iot_Bluetooth_oled.rst:56
msgid "Select **Arduino UNO R4 Minima** and the right port, then click **Upload**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/14-iot_Bluetooth_oled.rst:58
msgid "Open the Serial Monitor at **115200**. You should read:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/14-iot_Bluetooth_oled.rst:66
msgid "If you read ``[!] no reply from the module``, the module is not answering on D0/D1 - check the four wires and the power supply."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/14-iot_Bluetooth_oled.rst:70
msgid "3. Send Text from the Phone"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/14-iot_Bluetooth_oled.rst:72
msgid "Open LightBlue, tap **Scan** and connect to **SunFounder-C2**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/14-iot_Bluetooth_oled.rst:74
msgid "Expand the service **0xA002** and open the characteristic **C304**. Then tap **Write new value**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/14-iot_Bluetooth_oled.rst:79
msgid "Set the format in the top right corner to **UTF-8 String** and type ``Hello``. The picture shows the field just before sending:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/14-iot_Bluetooth_oled.rst:84
msgid "Send it. The word appears on the OLED and in the Serial Monitor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/14-iot_Bluetooth_oled.rst:86
msgid "Send another word - it replaces the first one, the display does not scroll."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/14-iot_Bluetooth_oled.rst:90
msgid "Two rules decide when the message is complete: either you end it with ``#``, or you simply stop typing. The sketch waits **120 ms** of silence and then treats what it has as one message."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/14-iot_Bluetooth_oled.rst:94
msgid "The display is 21 characters wide and 4 lines high. Longer text is cut off."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/14-iot_Bluetooth_oled.rst:98
msgid "4. Code explanation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/14-iot_Bluetooth_oled.rst:100
msgid "**The display**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/14-iot_Bluetooth_oled.rst:112
msgid "``0x3C`` is the I2C address of the module. Nothing shows up until ``display.display()`` is called - the sketch writes into a buffer first and pushes the buffer to the screen in one go."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/14-iot_Bluetooth_oled.rst:116
msgid "**Deciding when the text is finished**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/14-iot_Bluetooth_oled.rst:127
msgid "A ``#`` finishes the message at once. A line ending does the same, because some apps add one automatically."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/14-iot_Bluetooth_oled.rst:130
msgid "**The 120 ms rule**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/14-iot_Bluetooth_oled.rst:138
msgid "BLE sends the characters of one write in a burst, with almost no gap. When the burst stops, 120 ms pass and the sketch shows what it has. This makes typing on the phone feel natural without pressing anything."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/14-iot_Bluetooth_oled.rst:142
msgid "**Clearing afterwards**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/14-iot_Bluetooth_oled.rst:148
msgid "Without this the next word would be appended to the old one and the display would grow longer and longer until it is cut off."
msgstr ""
